From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: do not wait for a rootPD restart under the group mutex

ath12k_ahb_power_up() waited up to 30 s for a crashed rootPD to restart.
Recovery power-ups run under ag->mutex, so for that long remove, the
userPD fatal path and the reset work of every partner were blocked, for
each AHB device of the group whose rootPD crashed, in turn.

Wait in the reset work instead: after the power-down and before the
device is marked as powered down, without ag->mutex. The group power-up
cannot run meanwhile, because recovery_wait_power_down is still set.
Remove ends the wait early.

The waiter does not touch the crash marker; only the power-up consumes
it. rootpd_ready becomes complete_all(), so that waiting does not use it
up and it says whether the rootPD is up until the next crash resets it.
A crash during the wait therefore cannot have its marker cleared by the
waiter.

The AFTER_POWERUP notifier takes ag->mutex right after completing
rootpd_ready and finds the marker still set. If it then queued a group
recovery, a partner already down would start a new reset run that waits
20 s for the round in progress and tears it down if the round takes
longer. It now queues nothing while the device of that rootPD has
recovery_wait_power_down set: that device's reset work leads to the group
power-up, which picks the restart up.

ath12k_ahb_power_up() no longer waits. If the rootPD still has not
restarted (the wait timed out, or the rootPD crashed after this device
finished its reset work), it returns -ETIMEDOUT and leaves the marker
set. In a recovery the group then retries as for any failed power-up,
bounded by fail_cont_count, and the notifier queues a recovery once the
rootPD is up. First bring-up has no retry, so ath12k_core_soc_create()
waits before its power-up as well, under ag->mutex as that path always
ran; a rootPD that does not come back within 30 s fails the probe, as
before.

ag->mutex is still held across the rest of the power-up, as for every
recovery power-up: firmware load and authentication, and the userPD
spawn and ready waits (up to 5 s and 10 s).

Signed-off-by: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -376,19 +376,19 @@ static int ath12k_ahb_power_up(struct at
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
-	 * A recovery power-up can run before remoteproc has finished
-	 * restarting a crashed rootPD (for example while the rootPD dump is
-	 * still being collected). Booting the userPD then fails. Wait for the
-	 * restart and only then consume the crash marker, so the
-	 * QCOM_SSR_AFTER_POWERUP notifier still knows a recovery is owed if
-	 * this wait times out. Recovery power-ups run under ag->mutex, which
-	 * the notifier takes only after completing rootpd_ready.
+	 * A power-up can run before remoteproc has finished restarting a
+	 * crashed rootPD (for example while the rootPD dump is still being
+	 * collected). Booting the userPD then fails. Recovery power-ups run
+	 * under ag->mutex, so do not wait here: callers wait first, through
+	 * ath12k_hif_recovery_wait(). If the restart is still missing, fail
+	 * and leave the crash marker set (only this check consumes it). In a
+	 * recovery that failure queues a retry of the group, and the
+	 * QCOM_SSR_AFTER_POWERUP notifier still knows a recovery is owed; at
+	 * first bring-up it fails the probe.
 	 */
 	if (READ_ONCE(ab_ahb->rootpd_crashed)) {
-		time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ab_ahb->rootpd_ready,
-							ATH12K_ROOTPD_RECOVERY_TIMEOUT);
-		if (!time_left) {
-			ath12k_err(ab, "rootPD did not restart after crash, cannot boot userPD\n");
+		if (!completion_done(&ab_ahb->rootpd_ready)) {
+			ath12k_err(ab, "rootPD has not restarted after crash, cannot boot userPD\n");
 			return -ETIMEDOUT;
 		}
 		WRITE_ONCE(ab_ahb->rootpd_crashed, false);
@@ -615,6 +615,26 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_power_down(struct
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * Wait for a crashed rootPD to restart. The reset work calls this without
+ * ag->mutex, so that remove, a userPD fatal IRQ and partner resets are not held
+ * up, and the group power-up cannot run meanwhile because the device is marked
+ * as waiting (recovery_wait_power_down). First bring-up calls it under
+ * ag->mutex, which is safe: the notifier completes rootpd_ready before it takes
+ * the mutex. Remove completes rootpd_ready to end the wait early.
+ */
+static void ath12k_ahb_recovery_wait(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+{
+	struct ath12k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab);
+
+	if (!READ_ONCE(ab_ahb->rootpd_crashed))
+		return;
+
+	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ab_ahb->rootpd_ready,
+					 ATH12K_ROOTPD_RECOVERY_TIMEOUT))
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "rootPD did not restart after crash\n");
+}
+
 static void ath12k_ahb_init_qmi_ce_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_qmi_ce_cfg *cfg = &ab->qmi.ce_cfg;
@@ -838,6 +858,7 @@ static const struct ath12k_hif_ops ath12
 	.map_service_to_pipe = ath12k_ahb_map_service_to_pipe,
 	.power_up = ath12k_ahb_power_up,
 	.power_down = ath12k_ahb_power_down,
+	.recovery_wait = ath12k_ahb_recovery_wait,
 };
 
 static void ath12k_ahb_log_userpd_crash_reason(struct ath12k_base *ab)
@@ -963,13 +984,15 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_release_crashed_u
  * that is already in flight cannot absorb a crash that happens during its
  * own power-up, so every device is (re)queued; ath12k_core_reset()
  * serialises re-entry through reset_count/reset_complete.
- * False when the rootPD has finished restarting. A recovery power-up that
- * was waiting for it holds ag->mutex and consumes rootpd_crashed, so the
- * marker is re-checked under the mutex: if it is still set, no power-up
- * picked the restart up (none ran yet, or it timed out) and recovery is
- * still owed.
- * In both cases every device's reset is requested and its work queued,
- * also when it is queued or running already: a run whose request was
+ * False when the rootPD has finished restarting. A recovery power-up consumes
+ * rootpd_crashed under ag->mutex, so the marker is re-checked under the mutex:
+ * if it is clear, a power-up picked the restart up. Nothing is queued either
+ * if this device's reset is still on its way to the group power-up
+ * (recovery_wait_power_down): a new run of a partner could only wait for that
+ * round, and tear it down if the round outlasts the 20 s wait. Otherwise
+ * recovery is still owed.
+ * When recovery is queued, every device's reset is requested and its work
+ * queued, also when it is queued or running already: a run whose request was
  * answered by a later group power-up, or that finds no request, returns
  * at once (ath12k_core_reset()), so an extra run costs nothing.
  */
@@ -984,7 +1007,8 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_queue_group_recov
 		return;
 
 	mutex_lock(&ag->mutex);
-	if (!new_crash && !READ_ONCE(ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab)->rootpd_crashed))
+	if (!new_crash && (!READ_ONCE(ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab)->rootpd_crashed) ||
+			   ab->recovery_wait_power_down))
 		goto out;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ag->num_devices; i++) {
@@ -1017,7 +1041,8 @@ static int ath12k_ahb_root_pd_state_noti
 	switch (event) {
 	case QCOM_SSR_AFTER_POWERUP:
 		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_AHB, "Root PD is UP\n");
-		complete(&ab_ahb->rootpd_ready);
+		/* all: done stays set, waiting does not use it up, until a crash */
+		complete_all(&ab_ahb->rootpd_ready);
 		if (READ_ONCE(ab_ahb->rootpd_crashed))
 			ath12k_ahb_queue_group_recovery(ab, false);
 		return NOTIFY_OK;
@@ -1412,6 +1437,9 @@ static void ath12k_ahb_remove_prepare(st
 	set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_UNREGISTERING, &ab->dev_flags);
 	mutex_unlock(&ab->ag->mutex);
 
+	/* a reset work waiting for a rootPD restart need not wait any longer */
+	complete_all(&ath12k_ab_to_ahb(ab)->rootpd_ready);
+
 	cancel_work_sync(&ab->reset_work);
 	cancel_work_sync(&ab->restart_work);
 	cancel_work_sync(&ab->qmi.event_work);
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -866,6 +866,8 @@ static int ath12k_core_soc_create(struct
 
 	ath12k_debugfs_soc_create(ab);
 
+	ath12k_hif_recovery_wait(ab);
+
 	ret = ath12k_hif_power_up(ab);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_err(ab, "failed to power up :%d\n", ret);
@@ -2049,6 +2051,9 @@ reset:
 
 	ath12k_hif_power_down(ab, false);
 
+	/* Not under ag->mutex: this can take a while. */
+	ath12k_hif_recovery_wait(ab);
+
 	/* prepare for power up */
 	ab->qmi.num_radios = U8_MAX;
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/hif.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/hif.h
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/hif.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/hif.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ struct ath12k_hif_ops {
 	void (*stop)(struct ath12k_base *ab);
 	int (*power_up)(struct ath12k_base *ab);
 	void (*power_down)(struct ath12k_base *ab, bool is_suspend);
+	void (*recovery_wait)(struct ath12k_base *ab);
 	int (*suspend)(struct ath12k_base *ab);
 	int (*resume)(struct ath12k_base *ab);
 	int (*map_service_to_pipe)(struct ath12k_base *ab, u16 service_id,
@@ -141,6 +142,13 @@ static inline int ath12k_hif_power_up(st
 	return ab->hif.ops->power_up(ab);
 }
 
+/* Wait for what the device needs before a power-up can succeed. */
+static inline void ath12k_hif_recovery_wait(struct ath12k_base *ab)
+{
+	if (ab->hif.ops->recovery_wait)
+		ab->hif.ops->recovery_wait(ab);
+}
+
 static inline void ath12k_hif_power_down(struct ath12k_base *ab, bool is_suspend)
 {
 	if (!ab->hif.ops->power_down)
